  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Irish Poker (Drinking/Social). 2-10 players, 52-card deck. Setup: 4 face-down cards per player. Rounds: 1-Red/Black (guess color), 2-Higher/Lower (vs card 1), 3-Inside/Outside (vs cards 1-2), 4-Suit (guess suit). Scoring: Correct round = give drinks 2,4,6,8. Wrong = take drinks. Social winner: lowest total drinks.',
    Player: 'Welcome to Irish Poker, the ultimate prediction game. You have 4 face-down cards. Round 1: Guess Red or Black on card 1 (give/take 2 drinks). Round 2: Higher or Lower than card 1 on card 2 (give/take 4). Round 3: Inside or Outside the first two on card 3 (give/take 6). Round 4: Guess the Suit of card 4 (give/take 8). Strategy: Remember your cards and use probability!',
    objective: 'Correctly guess the attributes of your four hidden cards to avoid penalties (taking drinks) and assign rewards (giving drinks).',
    gameplay: "1. **Round 1 (Red or Black)**: Guess the color of your first card. Correct = Give 2 drinks; Wrong = Take 2.\n2. **Round 2 (Higher or Lower)**: Guess if your second card is higher or lower than the first. Correct = Give 4; Wrong = Take 4.\n3. **Round 3 (Inside or Outside)**: Guess if your third card's value is between or outside the first two. Correct = Give 6; Wrong = Take 6.\n4. **Round 4 (Suit)**: Guess the specific suit of your final card. Correct = Give 8; Wrong = Take 8.",
    keyRules: [
      'Follow the legal action constraints defined for Irish Poker.',
      'Round outcome is resolved by the scoring method: Scoring summary: Players predict card attributes and give/take drinks based on correctness.',
      'Winning condition: Correctly guess the attributes of your four hidden cards to avoid penalties (taking drinks) and assign rewards (giving drinks).',
    ],
